Ordinary Bayer used a physical-size viewport and an anchored scaled quad,
while statistics covered the complete RAW sensor. A 16:9 preview clipped
part of a 4:3 sensor without clipping its white-balance/exposure samples.

Use the existing aligned crop/texture helpers for all Bayer layouts, and
render that exact crop into the output-sized FBO. Quad-cell sampling stays
sensor-specific. No per-scene colour gains or JPEG tint are introduced.

